<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Final War of the Roman Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">32–<a href="/years/30-bce">30 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as War of Actium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Final War of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> was the civil war of 32–30 BCE between Octavian and the alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleopatra-vii">Cleopatra VII</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Octavian's fleet under Agrippa won the decisive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-actium">Battle of Actium</a> in 31 BCE, and Antony and Cleopatra took their own lives at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> in 30 BCE. Egypt was annexed, and Octavian, named Augustus in 27 BCE, became the first Roman emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/final-war-of-the-roman-republic.jpg" alt="Final War of the Roman Republic" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laureys a Castro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castro_Battle_of_Actium.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
